A background job keeps the worker's environment

Why: BackgroundJob::run() hands proc_open an environment array, which replaces the whole environment: a job sees BACKGROUND_JOB_ID and nothing else. It then misses every MISP_SETTING_* setting that EnvSetting reads, so it runs with other settings than the worker and the web tier, and it misses PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR with the worker's memory limit.
Upstream: not filed yet

diff --git a/app/Lib/Tools/BackgroundJobs/BackgroundJob.php b/app/Lib/Tools/BackgroundJobs/BackgroundJob.php
--- a/app/Lib/Tools/BackgroundJobs/BackgroundJob.php
+++ b/app/Lib/Tools/BackgroundJobs/BackgroundJob.php
@@ -86,7 +86,9 @@ class BackgroundJob implements JsonSerializable
             $descriptorSpec,
             $pipes,
             null,
-            ['BACKGROUND_JOB_ID' => $this->id]
+            // An array replaces the whole environment: the job keeps the worker's, so it
+            // reads the MISP_SETTING_* settings (EnvSetting) and the worker's PHP settings
+            ['BACKGROUND_JOB_ID' => $this->id] + getenv()
         );
 
         $this->pool($process, $pipes, $runningCallback);
